    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557-a8">

                <pb facs="0623" n="543" xml:id="pg543"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 5.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The governor-general to Mr.
                            Satow, British vice-consul.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Van</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-05-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 15,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In reply to your dispatch of May 14, 1902, we can testify that Dr. Ussher is a
                    good doctor and is permitted to carry on his profession in our land. His ability
                    we recognized during my son’s sickness, when I called him and saw the good
                    results of his treatment. I would not hesitate to testify to his ability, and,
                    furthermore, his excellency the military commander testifies that he had been
                    suffering for many years with a bad cough and other ailments, of which he had
                    been unable to rid himself. One day, taking his wife’s doctor, he called upon
                    Dr. Ussher at his dispensary and received relief by the treatment and medicines
                    Dr. Ussher had given him.</p>
                <p>These are facts that none can deny, but the province can not say anything in
                    regard to the report handed in by the municipality doctor and his
                    associates.</p>
                <p>(Seal of the governor-general.)</p>
            </div>
